      "tiny_5_mm_planktonic_photopositive_par": "Tiny (< 5 mm), planktonic, photopositive. Paralarvae drift in surface currents and feed on small zooplankton. Mortality is extreme — >99% of paralarvae do not survive to settlement. The few that do settle to substrate at 2-3 months age + ~10 mm size, where they begin benthic adult-style life.",
      "tiny_beautiful_and_one_of_the_most_ven": "Tiny, beautiful, and one of the most venomous animals on Earth. Four named species — H. lunulata, H. maculosa, H. fasciata, H. nierstraszi — all share the iconic blue ring display when threatened.",
      "tiny_bobtail_squid_some_symbiotic_with": "Tiny bobtail squid; some symbiotic with V. fischeri (like Euprymna).",
      "tiny_squid_3_5cm_symbiotic_vibrio_fisc": "Tiny squid (3-5cm). Symbiotic Vibrio fischeri bacteria glow on its ventral side to match downwelling moonlight, hiding its silhouette from below. At night, automatic counter-illumination boosts camo 50%. Tiny + fragile but invisible to night predators.",
      "tiny_squid_with_internal_spiral_chambe": "Tiny squid with INTERNAL spiral chambered shell — sole survivor of an ancient cephalopod lineage.",
