      "end_of_day": "End of day",
      "eric_foner_tom_paine_and_revolutionary": "Eric Foner, \"Tom Paine and Revolutionary America\" (1976)",
      "every_serious_shop_had_a_mark_called_a": "Every serious shop had a mark, called a \"device\" or colophon. It went on the title page and the last page. It signaled who printed the book, which mattered when (a) buyers wanted quality and (b) authorities wanted accountability. The dolphin-and-anchor was so successful Aldus Manutius spent half his career suing counterfeiters.",
      "explicit_historical_parallels_between_": "Explicit historical parallels between print and modern social media.",
      "falmouth_district_of_maine_january_1_1": "Falmouth, District of Maine · January 1, 1785",
      "falmouth_gazette_1785_reproduction": "Falmouth Gazette (1785) reproduction",
      "falmouth_gazette_and_weekly_advertiser_2": "Falmouth Gazette and Weekly Advertiser",
      "festina_lente_make_haste_but_slowly_a_": "“Festina lente — make haste, but slowly. A pocket book that pirates copy is still my book.”",
      "field_trip": "Field trip",
